        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.084,
            0.883,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Who do you think is correct? All of them are correct (Fig. 5.9). Then, why are their observations different? They are locating the distances of the school and garden from their houses. If, instead, each of them had thought of distances from a same object or point, say, the bus stand, then their observations would have been the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.206,
            0.882,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When distance is stated with respect to a fixed object or point, then this point is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "reference point.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.247,
            0.882,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A few days later, Hardeep tells his friends excitedly, “Let us all go to the playground. The sports teacher wants us to help her to draw lines with chuna powder (limestone powder) for making the Kabaddi court for the sports day.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
